  <sharedRules>
    <rule id="52ad-1981-b887-c66b" name="Spanish (Hannibal) - List Notes" publicationId="fc9f-8438-629b-e92d" hidden="false">
      <description>SPANISH ARMY LIST (Hannibal &amp; the Punic Wars, pp.70-73)
Northern Spanish tribes may be represented using the Gallic list. Characters up to 25%; the army must have one character as the overall leader; besides a General it may have an Army Standard Bearer and additional Heroic Leaders. If no Army General is selected the commander must be a Heroic Leader.
Terrain: the Spanish player may place his generated terrain on his opponent's side of the table. Ambush: before deployment the Spanish player may hide one unit anywhere out of sight of the enemy deployment zone and deploy it at the start of his first turn.
Optional rules (p.73, with consent): Sertorius and other revolts (field up to a quarter of points from the Roman list; Roman characters up to the character allowance; no Praetorian Guard, Lanciarii, Auxiliaries, Marines, Camelry or Elephants); Amphibious Caetrati (bladders +1 pt per model let Caetrati cross rivers and lakes).

ARMY COMPOSITIONS:
[Spanish - Iberians]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Special Units: up to 25%
  Infantry: Scutarii, Tribesmen, Caetrati. Cavalry: 0-1 Heavy Cavalry, Light Cavalry. Special Units: Slingers, Balearic Slingers, Celtiberian Warriors.
[Spanish - Celtiberians]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Special Units: up to 10%
  Infantry: Celtiberian Warriors, Tribesmen, Caetrati. Cavalry: 0-1 Heavy Cavalry, Light Cavalry. Special Units: Slingers.
[Spanish - Lusitanians]
  Characters: up to 25%
  Infantry: at least 50%
  Cavalry: up to 25%
  Special Units: up to 10%
  Infantry: Lusitanians and Caetrati (one unit of Lusitanians for every two units of Caetrati; no Caetrati unit may outnumber the smallest Lusitanian unit). Cavalry: 0-1 Heavy Cavalry, Light Cavalry (may have light armour +2). Special Units: Slingers.</description>
    </rule>
  </sharedRules>
</catalogue>
